diff --git a/.env.example b/.env.example
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..bc56aaa
--- /dev/null
+++ b/.env.example
@@ -0,0 +1,12 @@
+# Copy this file to .env and fill in your values. .env is gitignored — never commit real keys.
+
+# Cloudflare dashboard → R2 → Manage API tokens → create a token scoped to this bucket.
+R2_ACCOUNT_ID=
+R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
+R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
+R2_BUCKET_NAME=
+
+# The custom domain (or r2.dev URL) you've put in front of the bucket so files are
+# publicly reachable. Used both by the upload script (to print URLs) and by the site
+# itself as the default MEDIA_BASE_URL (src/config.ts).
+PUBLIC_MEDIA_BASE_URL=https://media.hexadecilab.com
diff --git a/MEDIA_GUIDE.md b/MEDIA_GUIDE.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..bab42e8
--- /dev/null
+++ b/MEDIA_GUIDE.md
@@ -0,0 +1,72 @@
+# Adding Films & Photos
+
+Two new content collections sit alongside `blog` and `projects`: `films` and `photos`.
+They're not split into `en`/`fr` folders — captions are short and the media speaks for itself.
+
+## Adding a photo
+
+Create `src/content/photos/my-photo.mdx`:
+
+```md
+---
+title: "Rising for air"
+description: "A freediver ascending toward the surface."
+date: 2026-08-02
+location: "Mediterranean Sea"
+tags:
+  - Freediving
+  - Underwater
+image: "../images/my-photo.jpg"        # local file → Astro optimizes it
+# image: "https://media.hexadecilab.com/photos/my-photo.jpg"   # or point straight at R2
+featured: true    # show on the homepage teaser grid
+draft: false
+---
+```
+
+Local images placed in `src/content/images/` get resized/converted to webp automatically by
+`astro:assets`. If you'd rather serve the untouched original (no re-compression at all), skip the
+local copy and put the R2 URL directly in `image:`.
+
+## Adding a film
+
+Create `src/content/films/my-film.mdx`:
+
+```md
+---
+title: "Alps Roadtrip"
+description: "A few days on the road through mountain passes."
+date: 2026-08-15
+location: "Alps, FR · IT · CH"
+duration: "06:24"
+gear: "DJI Action 6"
+tags:
+  - Kitesurf
+  - Watersport
+cover: "../images/my-film-cover.jpg"    # poster/thumbnail — can be a still frame
+videoUrl: "https://media.hexadecilab.com/films/my-film.mp4"
+featured: true
+draft: false
+---
+
+Optional longer write-up / behind-the-scenes notes go here, rendered as the film's article body.
+```
+
+`videoUrl` is played back with a plain `<video>` tag (see `src/components/media/video-player.astro`)
+— no YouTube/Vimeo re-encode, so whatever you upload is exactly what visitors get.
+
+## Media hosting workflow (R2)
+
+1. Shoot, cull/organize privately with something like **Immich** (self-hosted, great for reviewing
+   raw footage — not meant to be your public gallery though).
+2. Export your final cuts/edits at full quality.
+3. Upload the finished files to a **Cloudflare R2** bucket. R2 has no egress fees, which matters
+   once people start actually watching/downloading video.
+4. Put a custom domain in front of the bucket (e.g. `media.hexadecilab.com`) via a Cloudflare
+   Worker or R2's built-in custom domain support, and use that as `MEDIA_BASE_URL` in
+   `src/config.ts` / in each entry's `videoUrl` / `image`.
+5. If you want adaptive-quality streaming instead of a single flat file, look at **PeerTube** —
+   it supports S3-compatible storage (R2) natively and can sit in front of the bucket, and you'd
+   swap the `<video>` tag for an embed of the PeerTube player.
+
+This keeps the "manager" (Immich for private review, optionally PeerTube for public streaming)
+separate from the blog itself — the Astro site just needs a URL.
